{"resourceIdentifier":"2339","resourceName":"TIST Program in Uganda, VCS-CCB 010","description":"The International Small Group and Tree Planting Program (TIST) is a combined reforestation and sustainable development project in Uganda, carried out by subsistence farmers. The farmers plant trees on their land and retain ownership of the trees and their products. They receive training from TIST and a share of the carbon revenues from CAAC. \r\n\r\nThis project description (PD) is for a subset of the TIST project in Uganda and initially applies to 789 Small Groups, 3,196 Participants, 2,605 Project Areas, and 2,414 hectares. The main species planted are pine, gravellia, and teak. TIST farmers use a mosaic restoration approach, planting on thousands of individual farms spread across the landscape.","location":{"latitude":3.073811,"longitude":32.237527},"inPublicCommentPeriod":false,"lastPublicCommentPeriod":{"startInclusive":"2020-11-18","endExclusive":"2020-12-19","endInclusive":"2020-12-18"},"attributes":[{"code":"PROJECT_ID","values":[{"type":"string","value":"2339"}]},{"code":"STATE_PROVINCE","values":[{"type":"string","value":"Multiple States/Provinces"}]}],"participationSummaries":[{"programCode":"VCS","attributes":[{"code":"PROPONENT_NAME","values":[{"type":"string","value":"Clean Air Action Corporation"},{"type":"string","value":"ME, United States"},{"type":"string","value":"918-747-8770"},{"type":"string","value":"https://program.tist.org/"}]},{"code":"PROJECT_STATUS","values":[{"type":"string","value":"Registered"},{"type":"assetSearchLink","value":null,"targetId":"2339"},{"type":"bufferSearchLink","value":null,"targetId":"2339"}]},{"code":"EST_ANNUAL_EMISSION_REDCT","values":[{"type":"string","value":"83340"}]},{"code":"TOTAL_BUFFER_POOL_CREDITS","values":[{"type":"integer","value":17313}]},{"code":"PRIMARY_PROJECT_CATEGORY_NAME","values":[{"type":"string","value":"Agriculture Forestry and Other Land Use"}]},{"code":"PROJECT_SUBCATERGORY_NAMES","values":[{"typ